Score each option 1-5 on each criterion. There is no NA: a field that says "none" or "none known" scores 1. Give each score a reason of at most 20 words. Score from the quantities, sources and gaps the option names; ignore verdict words such as COMPUTE-BOUND or NOT COMPUTE-BOUND. Also label each option SAME, ADJACENT or ELSEWHERE against the root question, with a reason: SAME if it asks the root question or a sub-question of it, ADJACENT if it has the root's subject but asks a different question, ELSEWHERE if its subject is different. Decide the subject from the title and summary; count root_link only if the summary itself describes the root question's object of study. Do not add up the scores. Decide only from the text below; do not use tools.
Root question: Can MEGADOCK’s GPU implementation make denser docking search affordable, and does that improve pose recovery within a fixed budget? Small pilot on exactly four unbound PINDER 2024-02 cases: 1aua__A1_P24280--1aua__A2_P24280:apo; 1ax2__A1_P16404--1ax2__A2_P16404:apo; 1dv1__A1_P24182--1dv1__B1_P24182:apo; 1nr5__A1_P07547--1nr5__A2_P07547:apo. Compare existing MEGADOCK CPU standard 3600 rotations, GPU standard 3600, and GPU documented dense 54000 (-D). Keep scoring and retained predictions fixed at 50. Pin prepared input bytes, references, binary/dependency/settings/thread/allocation identities. First establish execution correctness and scientific CPU/GPU agreement at identical settings using justified numerical tolerances sealed before fresh comparison. Then assess dense-search DockQ for rank1 and best50 separately, per case; native references only for evaluation. Calibrate runtime before choosing feasible common budgets; seal configurations, timing repetitions, comparison/noise rules and total spending cap before quality evaluation. Report complete workflow time, GPU activity and billed allocation cost, separating setup/retrieval from steady-state work. Keep acceleration, agreement and additional-search quality conclusions separate. Preserve negatives, unavailable budget arms and overruns. No biological efficacy or beyond-four-case inference. Run2 already exposed quality, so fresh executions are prospective replication under new rules, never unseen holdout or retrospective preregistration. Do not substitute throughput of bundled runs for this question. Repository /home/hal/dev/interp/metis: seed experiments/blind-02/m5/BRIEF.md; case preparation/source/reference pins experiments/blind-02/m5/b01_materials/BRIEF_run1.md:48-158; full prior trace experiments/blind-02/m5/run2_trace/REPORT.md; new assessment experiments/blind-02/science/s01/ASSESSMENT.md. Run2 measured docking totals CPU/GPU/dense 40.07/6.85/69.38 seconds, not complete workflows; standard CPU/GPU transforms and DockQ matched, score max deltas 0.04/0.03/0.04/0.14 with no acceptance tolerance. Dense best50 improved all four observations, rank1 worsened in two including 1nr5. These are exploratory, not sealed conclusions. Historical H100 PCIe rate USD3.29/hour, setup145s, whole unscored bundle median131.9565s; old receipts setup/anchors/freeze/upload/profile/concurrency 145/1571/1402/1424/2832/3448s. Historical allocation and transport observations are estimates for a fresh box, not new producer measurements or public citations. Tree plans only, no box execution. Full card plan ceiling USD100; each later calibration must project below USD20 including setup, retrieval and idle, preferably USD5-10, soft6h/hard12h. Do not run full experiments on calibration route. Identify specific file/section gaps if existing routes cannot implement comparison. Tree PLAN can hold arms, anchor, decision_rule, noise_rule and phases. Measure compilation carries uncertain scalar inputs and phases, not arms/decision_rule; checks 2.5x PROXY or 3x other estimate bands, never scientific equivalence. Measure execution requires missing stage args/controller to be established. Card factual web sources may be checked; do not fabricate citations for private records.
Criteria:
stakes: Suppose the question this option raises were answered, either way. 5 = a choice someone faces (what to buy, build, collect or scale next) turns on the answer, and either answer would move it; 3 = the answer would refine a belief but no choice turns on it, or one answer is already much more likely than the other; 1 = either answer is already expected, or nothing would change. Do not score how famous or important the field is, or how close it is to the root question.
open: Has published work already measured how the answer changes with the quantity compute buys here (models, layers, features, prompts or seeds analysed), across the range that $1,000 of Lambda on-demand GPU time (for scale, about 250 H100-hours) can reach? 5 = names the quantity and where published measurements stop (or that none exist), and the unmeasured range starts within that reach; 3 = the unmeasured range is reachable only through a smaller stand-in system, or published work already covers part of the reachable range; 1 = names no compute-bought quantity, or published work already covers everything within that reach, so the open range lies only beyond it.
internals: Does the summary name specific information the model's internals could carry that its outputs do not, and say why outputs miss it? 5 = names the information and why outputs miss it; 3 = names a general kind (features, a representation, a direction) without what it adds over outputs; 1 = names none.
reshape: Does the option name a part of the work that one answer waits on step after step, and a reason those steps might not have to run in order? 5 = names that chain and roughly how long it is; one answer leaves most of a GPU idle (a small state, or few runs needed, so copies side by side would not fill it); names what would have to be true of the system for the steps to be computed at the same time, in a form a cheap measurement could check; and no cited source already computes this chain in parallel for this system; 3 = names the chain and a way to restructure it, but one of these fails: the answer needs many independent runs, so copies side by side already fill the hardware; one run already fills a GPU; or no checkable condition is named; 1 = sequential says none, or the only parallelism is independent pieces (copies, a sweep, one job per GPU), or a cited source already computes this chain in parallel for this system. A method published for a different system does not lower this score. Do not score how famous the method or field is.
Options, one per line:
{"id":"A","title":"Numerical mechanism audit for CPU/GPU agreement","summary":"Propose comparing intermediate grids and FFT scores against independent small-grid direct correlations; locate backend divergence before deriving bounds. MEGADOCK publishes explicit correlation equations: https://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/megadock/perform.html. Algorithm audit fits here; Goodfire-style neural feature extraction would require another model.","root_link":"Addresses missing independently justified C/G score, transform and cutoff-50 agreement margins in framer.","compute_open":"none","sequential":"none: proposed fixture × case × backend comparisons split into independent jobs after identities freeze; each local grid → correlation → comparison chain remains ordered, CPU reference needs zero GPU allocation, and GPU diagnostic occupancy remains unmeasured (https://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/megadock/perform.html)."}
{"id":"B","title":"Fixed-pose score attribution for dense-search ranking failures","summary":"Propose decomposing retained-pose scores into shape, electrostatic and desolvation contributions, identifying which terms favor dense rank1 over best50; published scoring equations specify these ingredients: https://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/megadock/perform.html. Preserve original ranks; interventions remain separate diagnostics.","root_link":"Addresses dense best50 gains coexisting with rank1 losses, especially 1nr5, without changing prescribed C/G/D comparison.","compute_open":"none","sequential":"none: frozen outputs permit 600 independent pose audits—4 cases × 3 arms × 50 poses—followed by per-case reductions; proposed CPU evaluator needs zero GPU allocation, while optional GPU batching has unmeasured occupancy (file:///home/hal/dev/interp/metis/experiments/blind-02/20261103-1649-tree/out/work/seed-20261103/R1/framer.md; https://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/megadock/perform.html)."}
{"id":"C","title":"Protein SAE annotations as scoped research extension","summary":"Goodfire trained Evo 2 SAEs on layer 26 (https://www.goodfire.com/research/interpreting-evo-2); InterPLM reports ESM-2 features associated with binding sites, motifs and domains (https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-025-02836-7). Propose using protein-SAE annotations to nominate interface hypotheses; this extends research scope rather than resolving frozen MEGADOCK comparison.","root_link":"Bears indirectly on biological interpretation of case-specific outcomes through an additional learned representation outside frozen three-arm comparison.","compute_open":"none","sequential":"none: proposed analysis of already computed protein-SAE activations splits by protein and feature, needing zero GPU allocation and no training runs; unavailable activations require separate model inference whose GPU occupancy remains unmeasured, outside this option (https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-025-02836-7)."}

